	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Westfall is a land of wide golden plains between {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link} and the Great Sea. For generations its farms filled the granaries of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}, and the folk of the capital called it their breadbasket. Now the fields lie untended. Windmills turn over empty barns, strange machines walk the furrows, and men in red masks rule the roads. Most of the farmers have gone. Those who remain have learned that no army is coming, and that they must defend their homes themselves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year when the first farmers ploughed the plains west of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. What is known is that the land was rich in more than grain. Beneath its hills lay mines and quarries that fed the forges of the capital, and the greatest of them, beneath the village of {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link}, was once the richest gold works in all the human lands. The coast gave fish to the villages and danger to the ships, and a lighthouse was raised on the southern rocks to guide sailors past them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Westfall belongs to the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link} in all but name. The Brotherhood holds {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link}, the mines and the southern hills. It drove the farmers from their homes, sometimes by threat and sometimes by fire, and it now works the land for its own ends. {link:riverpaw-gnolls}Riverpaw gnolls{/link} and {link:kobolds}kobolds{/link} labour in the mines at its command. {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} has sent no soldiers. Its army is marshalled far away, and the regent's court has answered the pleas of Westfall with silence. On {link:sentinel-hill}Sentinel Hill{/link}, a veteran named {link:gryan-stoutmantle}Gryan Stoutmantle{/link} has raised the People's Militia from farmers who refused to leave. They are few, but they are the only law in Westfall.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The farmers of Westfall.{/b} A handful of families, such as the Saldeans, hold their land against every danger. Others, like the Furlbrows, have packed what they could and turned toward the city.
• {b}The People's Militia.{/b} Former farmers and returned soldiers under {link:gryan-stoutmantle}Gryan Stoutmantle{/link}, sworn to defend the plains in the name of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link}.
• {b}The {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}.{/b} Thieves, smugglers and pillagers in red bandanas. The colour and cloth of the bandana mark a member's rank.
• {b}The {link:riverpaw-gnolls}Riverpaw gnolls{/link}.{/b} They raid the fields and dig in the {link:gold-coast-quarry}Gold Coast Quarry{/link} on behalf of the Brotherhood.
• {b}Murlocs.{/b} The {link:murlocs}murloc{/link} tribes swarm along the whole length of the coast.
• {b}The {link:harvest-golems}harvest golems{/link}.{/b} Machines built to tend the crops now drive off anyone who comes near them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Years of Plenty.{/b} Westfall's grain and gold made it one of the pillars of the kingdom.
• {b}The First War.{/b} When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} razed {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} in the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, the great gold mine beneath {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link} was abandoned. It took the name of the {link:the-deadmines}Deadmines{/link}.
• {b}The Betrayal of the Masons.{/b} After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the {link:stonemasons-guild}Stonemasons' Guild{/link} rebuilt the capital and was cheated of its wages by the {link:house-of-nobles}House of Nobles{/link}. Driven from the city, the masons came west under {link:edwin-vancleef}Edwin VanCleef{/link} and made Westfall their own.
• {b}The Abandonment.{/b} One by one, the farms fell. Stormwind did not answer. {link:gryan-stoutmantle}Gryan Stoutmantle{/link}, home from the ruin of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, began to gather those who would stand and fight.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Plains",
			text = [=[• The Brotherhood does not only steal farms. It steals their deeds as well, and it is said that its forgers can make a stolen deed serve a new master.
• Along {link:longshore}Longshore{/link} lie the wrecks of many ships. The sailors of the Great Sea still tell of a drowned captain who left a trail of clues to his hidden treasure.
• A ghost keeps the flame of the {link:westfall-lighthouse}Westfall Lighthouse{/link}. He died on the rocks below it, and he will not let another sailor share his fate.
• The farmers say that the fields of Westfall are sick, and that the sickness comes from beneath the ground.]=],
		},
	},
})

